--- E2g: PROOF (block algebra) ---
S'S'^T = (M'+I)(I-M') = I - M'^2  (M' skew).
Input skew-Hadamard of order n: M^2 = (1-n)I.
trP=0:    M'^2 = I2(x)(2M^2-I) = (2(1-n)-1) I = (1-2n) I  => S'S'^T = 2n I. QED
trP=+-2:  off-diag block of M'^2 = (a+d)(b M^2 + beta M) = +-2(b(1-n)I + beta M),
          diagonal entries -2ab(n-1) != 0 for n>=2 => M'^2 not scalar => fails. QED

--- E3: 2x2 DNA — sign-matrix trichotomy ---
P_A(T[K2])  = [[1,1],[1,1]]   = e e^T (e=(1,1)) : True, rank 1, det 0
P_C(SCblow) = [[1,-1],[-1,1]] = f f^T (f=(1,-1)): True, rank 1, det 0
P_B(D_skew) = [[1,1],[1,-1]]  = 2x2 Hadamard    : PP^T=2I True, det -2
P_A P_C = 0: True;  P_A + P_C = 2I: True;  H2 e = 2e1, H2 f = 2e2: [2, 0] [0, 2]

TRICHOTOMY: the three orbits = the three symmetric +-1 matrices mod symmetry:
  orbit A: P = +-e e^T  (2x projector on the SYMMETRIC line of the copy-swap)
  orbit C: P = +-f f^T  (2x projector on the ANTISYMMETRIC line)
  orbit B: P = 2x2 Hadamard (EXCHANGES the two swap-eigenlines), det = -2.
Equivalences (all verified above): rows of P orthogonal <=> trP=0 <=> detP=-2
  <=> P Hadamard <=> {P,Q}=0 <=> M'^2 block-diagonal <=> skew-Hadamard preserved.
Sing. members (det 0) are rank-1; the Hadamard is the UNIQUE invertible class.

--- E3b: spectral pencil — spec(M') = U_{lambda in spec M} spec(lambda P + Q) ---
(proof: M normal; on C^2 (x) eigvec(lambda), M' restricts to lambda P + Q;
 char poly check: det(xI - M') = prod_lambda [x^2 - (trP) lambda x + (detP lambda^2 + 1)])
pencil law (char-poly product) for all 16 members x 7 sample n=5 tournaments: True
det(lambda P + Q) = detP*lambda^2 + 1: lift-pair products are
  orbit A/C (detP=0):  product = 1   (unimodular 'boost' pair, lifts l' = a*l +- sqrt(l^2-1))
  orbit B  (detP=-2):  product = 1 - 2 lambda^2;  trace 0 => l'^2 = 2 lambda^2 - 1 = T2(lambda).

