--- E5: Clifford / Cayley-Dickson statement ---
THEOREM (2x2 DNA / Clifford classification). Every valid span{M,I} block
doubling is M' = P(x)M + Q(x)I with P symmetric +-1, Q = beta*J, beta=+-1.
M'^2 = P^2(x)M^2 + {P,Q}(x)M - I, with {P,Q} = beta*(trP)*J. The following are
equivalent: (i) {P,Q}=0; (ii) trP=0; (iii) P^2=2I (rows orthogonal, P Hadamard,
detP=-2); (iv) M'^2 = I2(x)(2M^2-I) for all T; (v) M'(T) preserves skew-Hadamard.
The pair (gamma+ = P/sqrt2, gamma- = Q) then satisfies gamma+^2=+1, gamma-^2=-1,
{gamma+,gamma-}=0: a real representation of the Clifford algebra Cl(1,1) ~ M2(R).

CAYLEY-DICKSON reading: M skew = 'purely imaginary' (zbar = -z). The CD twist
law j z = zbar j becomes Q(P(x)M) = (P(x)(-M))Q, i.e. {P(x)M, Q} = 0, i.e.
{P,Q} = 0 — the SAME condition. So the good doublings are exactly the CD steps
M' = sqrt2 * gamma+ (x) M + j (x) I, with j^2 = -1. D_skew = (1,1,-1,1) uses
P = H2 = [[1,1],[1,-1]] (standard unnormalized Hadamard/Sylvester convention)
and Q = +J (counterclockwise j); beta=-1 is the conjugate orientation -j;
a<->d swap = relabeling the two CD sheets; global negation = the opposite
algebra. The 8 orbit-B members = 2(orientation) x 2(sheet) x 2(op) copies of
ONE CD step. Repo connection (07-reflections/lrc-cayley-dickson-tower-s387.md:
'each recursive doubling closes one old freedom and exposes a new defect'):
the skew-Hadamard tower 1->2->4->8->... with tournament cores on 0,1,3,7,...
vertices is the R->C->H->O dimension ladder; D_skew is its matrix shadow, and
the rank-1 members (T[K2], SCblow) are the DEGENERATE pencils that stay inside
one swap-eigenline — they keep the boost (product-1) spectrum but lose the
Hadamard mixing, exactly a CD-style property loss.

